      "body": "Off Leash update 11/11/2026\nHappy Veterans’ Day!\n\nUKRAINE\n•Envoys from Russia, Ukraine, and the U.S. held nearly four hours of trilateral talks yesterday in Abu Dhabi. U.S. SecState Rubio called the meeting “very productive” and Ukraine’s Pres. Zelensky said it was “constructive and very substantive,” but there are no indications that it yielded any breakthroughs.\n•Meanwhile, experts estimate that Ukraine’s drone attacks on Russian refineries have reduced Russia’s oil refining capacity by about 30% in the past two weeks. Russia reintroduced petrol sales limits in response, while its Foreign Minister, Sergei Lavrov, whined that Ukraine was ignoring Pres. Trump’s calls to observe an energy ceasefire that would only benefit Russia.\n\nHAITI\n•El Salvador’s President Nayib Bukele said his troops had destroyed the headquarters of Haiti’s 400 Mawozo gang in its Croix-de-Bouquets stronghold.\n•The Miami Herald reported that the operation was a joint effort between Bukele’s Salvadoran troops and Haiti’s National Police drone task force, and that 400 Mawozo’s leader, Wilson \"Lanmò San Jou\" Joseph, wasn’t in the building at the time.\n\nIRAN\n•The U.S. withdrew at least 12 military refueling tanker planes from a second British airbase, RAF Mildenhall, citing Iranian threats similar to those that led to the withdrawal of U.S. bombers from RAF Fairford in September.\n•Separately (or maybe not), Iran’s Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC) said it had lifted its self-imposed 2,000 km (1,250 mi.) limit on the range of its ballistic missiles, with the ominous implication that it could start firing at targets beyond the Middle East. [But not all the way to the UK, which is about 4,500 km (2,800 mi.) from Iran: analysts estimate that IRGC missiles have a max. range of about 3,000 km (1,850 mi.).]\n\nVENEZUELA\n•ExxonMobil signed a memorandum of understanding to explore “potential upstream opportunities with Venezuela’s state-owned Petróleos de Venezuela. The possible partnership marks a clear reversal from Exxon’s CEO’s position in January, when its boss called Venezuela “uninvestable.”",
